@flexiarg baldwin/choose-the-heritable-unit-where-invariance-lives
@title Put the Heritable Unit Where the Invariance Is
@sigils [🌰/本]
@keywords representation, locus, context, coordinates, invariance, assimilation, metaca, indifference
@audience MetaCA designers, evolutionary-computation researchers, representation designers
@tone constructive
@style pattern
@childof baldwin/mechanism
@references [baldwin/stationarity-decides-what-can-be-fixed baldwin/assimilable-traits-need-heritable-shadows baldwin/metaca-negative-evidence-localizes-the-bottleneck]

! conclusion:
  "No assimilable structure exists" and "no assimilable structure exists in the
  coordinates I chose" are different findings, and only the second has been earned by
  the MetaCA measurements. Before concluding that a substrate cannot assimilate, look
  for the coordinate system in which the adaptive answer is invariant across lifetimes,
  and make *that* the heritable unit.

  + context:
    MetaCA's heritable unit is the lattice cell: a per-cell rule field and a per-cell
    hold mask. The corrected indifference measurement shows that per-cell agreement
    between live and frozen reads is unimodal (mean `0.290`, sd `0.089`) with no cell
    above `0.6`, spatially coherent within a run (lag-1 `+0.422`), and uncorrelated
    across initial conditions (`-0.010`, `-0.060`, `+0.111`). Structure exists; it is
    simply not indexed by cell.

  + IF:
    A per-unit assimilation scheme fails and the per-unit invariance measurement is flat
    or unstable across evaluations.

  + HOWEVER:
    Changing coordinates is also the easiest way to lose a diagnosis, and a
    representation search that changes the unit, the cost, the target and the operator
    together explains nothing. A new unit must be adopted as a registered hypothesis
    with its own invariance measurement, not as a hopeful redesign.

  + THEN:
    Re-index the invariance measurement you already have before building anything. Take
    the same live-versus-frozen agreement statistic and compute it per candidate unit —
    for MetaCA, the four-bit context quadruple the rewrite already conditions on, which
    has sixteen classes and recurs across initial conditions even when cells do not. If
    agreement is bimodal and cross-seed stable in the new index where it was unimodal
    and unstable in the old, the heritable unit has been located and the genome becomes
    a small evolvable table over that index.

  + BECAUSE:
    Selection can only fix what is the same in every lifetime the genome meets. A unit
    whose correct value is redrawn each evaluation is unfixable by construction, however
    good the operator, the cost, or the search budget. Conversely, an adaptive process
    that responds to recurring conditions has *some* invariant description; the design
    question is whether the genome is written in those terms.

    + EVIDENCE:
      Per-cell holding was selected against by six- to fourteen-fold relative to the
      mutation-only expectation of `0.1858`, horizontal transfer of contiguous cell
      segments moved dependence within noise, and coupled hold-plus-allele mutation did
      not differ qualitatively from independent mutation. Three operators over the same
      unit gave the same answer, which is what a wrong unit looks like rather than what
      an insufficient search looks like.

    + COUNTERFACTUAL:
      If context-indexed agreement is also unimodal and cross-seed unstable, the
      substrate has no invariant the genome could carry at any granularity, and the
      negative generalizes from the cell to the representation.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Re-index an existing invariance measurement before proposing a new genome.
    - Register the candidate unit and its invariance prediction as one claim.
    - Report the unit alongside every assimilation result, since the claim is relative to it.
